+        // The sender name is a display name the remote side supplies, and the only
+        // thing that ever removes a row is Stop(), which nothing calls after Start(),
+        // so both the key length and the row count are bounded here. A name longer
+        // than any real player name cannot belong to a proxy actor, and a full table
+        // drops the packet instead of growing without limit. The row cap matches
+        // MorphSyncService::kMaxRemoteSnapshots so both halves refuse the same peers.
+        constexpr std::size_t kMaxSenderNameBytes = 256;
